WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.048
Host: Predict the immediate effect of an
isolated afterload increase on a
pressure–volume loop.

2
00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:13.077
Guide: At unchanged preload and contractility,
the ventricle must develop more pressure
before ejection.

3
00:00:13.077 --> 00:00:16.151
Guide: It generally ejects less on that beat,

4
00:00:16.151 --> 00:00:20.240
Guide: leaving a larger end-systolic volume
and a narrower loop.

5
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.493
Guide: Later reflex and filling responses may
modify this.

6
00:00:24.493 --> 00:00:33.447
Host: In a simplified ventricle, end-diastolic
volume is 120 mL and end-systolic volume is 50
mL.

7
00:00:33.447 --> 00:00:35.751
Host: What is stroke volume?

8
00:00:35.751 --> 00:00:45.619
Guide: 70 mL. Subtract end-systolic from end-
diastolic volume: 120 minus 50 equals 70 mL.
